message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Heileman"
    given-names: "Grant David"
title: "apple-bottom: FP64-class BLAS for Apple Silicon GPUs"
version: 1.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
url: "https://github.com/grantdh/apple-bottom"
repository-code: "https://github.com/grantdh/apple-bottom"
keywords:
  - BLAS
  - GPU
  - Apple Silicon
  - Metal
  - Scientific Computing
  - High Performance Computing
  - Double Precision
  - Quantum ESPRESSO
license: MIT
abstract: >
  BLAS for Apple Silicon GPUs, which have no FP64 units. Each FP64 value is
  carried as an unevaluated sum of two FP32 values (double-float, about 48
  significant bits, ~1e-15 relative error per element) and the arithmetic runs
  in Metal compute shaders. DGEMM, ZGEMM and DSYRK are available through a C API
  with GPU-resident matrices, a device-buffer API and a drop-in BLAS ABI
  (dgemm_/zgemm_) for Fortran codes such as Quantum ESPRESSO, where each call is
  routed to the GPU or to Accelerate from measured end-to-end timings.
